    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the suite).\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key and duplicate/soft-match detection per the specification.\n\n**Identity key** \u2014 `Owner.getIdentityKey()` (`model/Owner.java`) now returns the lower-case full SHA-256 hex digest over `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)` (email absent \u2192 empty string), replacing the old plain `telephone|email|householdId` string.\n\nSupporting pieces, each a small single-responsibility unit:\n- **`model/Soundex.java`** (new) \u2014 American Soundex encoder (retained first letter + 3 digits, with the standard vowel/`h`/`w` adjacency rules), styled like the existing `LuhnCheckDigit`.\n- **`model/Sha256Hex.java`** \u2014 moved from `service` into `model` (a pure utility) so the entity can reuse it without a layering violation, and added a `lowerHex(...)` method for the full 64-char digest. The two service generators (`CustomerCodeGenerator`, `HouseholdIdGenerator`) now import it; no logic duplicated.\n\n**Duplicate 409** \u2014 unchanged wiring: `findOwnersByIdentityKey` (ignoring deleted owners) drives the 409, and the email-domain blocklist still runs first during email normalization, before the duplicate check.\n\n**Soft-match** \u2014 new `ClinicService.findSoftMatchOf(owner)` (replacing the retired `findHouseholdDuplicateOf`) finds a non-deleted owner sharing `soundex(lastName)` + postcode but with a *different* identity key. The controller now sets `possibleDuplicateOf` from it before saving. So two owners with the same last name and postcode but different telephones are created as a soft match, not rejected.\n\n**Retired dead code** \u2014 the spec's now-obsolete household-duplicate 409 path: removed `DuplicateHouseholdException`, its handler in `ExceptionControllerAdvice`, and `findHouseholdDuplicateOf`. (`householdId` itself stays \u2014 it still feeds household size / membership-level cap and is returned in the DTO.)\n\n**Docs** \u2014 updated the OpenAPI descriptions/example for `identityKey`, `possibleDuplicate`, and the now-ignored `sharesHousehold`, plus the corresponding Javadoc in `Owner`, to match the new behaviour.",
